-- National Insurance Law [Consolidated Version], s 348 (סכום מרבי, סכום מזערי וסכום שלא יובא בחשבון) —
-- the maximum, the minimum, and the amount not taken into account. Quotations (`src:N`) are copied
-- mechanically from line N of
-- ../../registers/source-bundle/national-insurance-law-consolidated-version-5755-1995.he.wiki.txt.
--
-- WHAT IT DOES, in the order this module applies it to an insured person's income for a period:
--   (a1) part of the income not from work is not taken into account;
--   (a)  income above the Schedule K maximum is not taken into account;
--   (b)  income below the Schedule K minimum is treated as the minimum;
--   (d), (e) for the unemployed, and for volunteers, yeshiva students and those in civil or
--        national-civic service, the income is treated as the item 3 minimum.
--   (c)  the Minister may change the minimum amounts by order.
-- The maximum is always above the minimum, so (a) and (b) cannot both bite and their order does not
-- matter; (a1) comes first because what it disregards is not "his income" for (a) and (b).
--
-- WHICH YEARS: contribution periods from January 2026 (NOTES.md, assumption A1). The tags תשפ״ה־11,
-- תשפ״ו and תשפ״ו־7 count to Amendments 7, 8 and 9 of the National-Civic Service Law, each of which
-- only moves that Law's expiry date (fetched 2026-10-06; NOTES.md section 7); they reach this section
-- through the date in the editors' note on (e)'s temporary text.

§ `Section 348 — maximum, minimum and disregarded amounts`
-- src:3762 | סעיף 348 – סכום מרבי, סכום מזערי וסכום שלא יובא בחשבון [תיקון: תשס״ב־7, תשס״ג־12, תשס״ו־8, תשס״ז־11, תשס״ח־5, תשע״ד־6, תשע״ו־8, תשע״ז־16, תשפ״ג־8, תשפ״ד־12, תשפ״ה־11, תשפ״ו, תשפ״ו־7]

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K (source lines 4751-4773): the figures given are for the case's tax year
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the figures given are for another tax year than the case` MEANS
    REFUSE "the figures given are for another tax year than the case"

§§ `The period of the case`

-- The first and last month of the period, for the dated arm of (e).
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN p IS A `A period under Schedule K`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the first month of the period` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a month of the tax year` m   THEN m
    WHEN `a quarter of the tax year` q THEN `the first month of` q
    WHEN `the whole tax year`          THEN 1

@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K, "רבעון" (source line 4771)
GIVEN p IS A `A period under Schedule K`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the last month of the period` p MEANS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `a month of the tax year` m   THEN m
    WHEN `a quarter of the tax year` q THEN `the first month of` q PLUS 2
    WHEN `the whole tax year`          THEN 12

-- A month counted from year 0, so that periods in different years compare.
GIVEN `the month` IS A NUMBER
      `the year`  IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the month count of month` `the month` `of` `the year` MEANS
    `the year` TIMES 12 PLUS `the month`

§§ `348(e) — the classes it names, with its permanent and its temporary text`

-- The consolidation prints (e) twice. The editors label the first "(the permanent text)" and the second
-- "(temporary provision until the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law, 5774-2014, on 31.8.2026;
-- it applies also to one who began service before that date, after that date too, until he completes
-- his service)". The temporary text names one class more, "one serving in national-civic service".
-- src:3768 | (ה) [note: (הנוסח הקבוע):] מתנדב בשירות לאומי או בהתנדבות קהילתית, תלמיד במוסד תורני או בישיבה או מי שמשרת בשירות אזרחי כהגדרתו בסעיף 6(א) לחוק דחיית שירות לתלמידי ישיבות שתורתם אומנותם, התשס״ב–2002, שאין לו הכנסה או שהכנסתו אינה מגיעה לסכום המזערי האמור בפרט 3 בלוח י״א, יראו כאילו הכנסתם היתה הסכום המזערי האמור.
-- src:3769 | [note: (הוראת שעה עד מועד הפקיעה של חוק שירות לאומי־אזרחי, התשע״ד–2014, ביום 31.8.2026, חלה גם על מי שהתחיל את שירותו לפני המועד האמור גם אחרי המועד האמור עד שייסים את שירותו):] מתנדב בשירות לאומי או בהתנדבות קהילתית, משרת בשירות לאומי–אזרחי, תלמיד במוסד תורני או בישיבה או מי שמשרת בשירות אזרחי כהגדרתו בסעיף 6(א) לחוק דחיית שירות לתלמידי ישיבות שתורתם אומנותם, התשס״ב–2002, שאין לו הכנסה או שהכנסתו אינה מגיעה לסכום המזערי האמור בפרט 3 בלוח י״א, יראו כאילו הכנסתם היתה הסכום המזערי האמור.
-- The date is the National-Civic Service Law's own expiry (its s 36(a)), which Amendments 7, 8 and 9
-- of that Law moved from 30.6.2025 to 15.11.2025, 31.3.2026 and 31.8.2026 (fetched 2026-10-06,
-- NOTES.md section 7). The editors' note is relied on for the date, as an aid (assumption A3);
-- whether a later amendment moved it again was not searched for.
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), editors' note to the temporary text (source line 3769); National-Civic Service Law (Amendment No. 9), 5786-2026, s 1
GIVETH A DATE
`the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law, which ends the temporary text of section 348(e)` MEANS
    YMD 2026 8 31

-- The classes both texts name. "civil service as defined in section 6(a) of the Deferral of Service
-- for Yeshiva Students Law" is that Law's definition, not the s 1 definition of "שירות אזרחי".
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), both texts (source lines 3768-3769)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(e) — the person is of a class both texts name` c MEANS
        c's `a volunteer in national service or in community volunteering`
    OR  c's `a student in a Torah institution or in a yeshiva`
    OR  c's `serving in civil service as defined in section 6(a) of the Deferral of Service for Yeshiva Students Law`

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), temporary text (source line 3769)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the temporary text of section 348(e) ends inside this period, and the person began national-civic service on or after the day it ends` MEANS
    REFUSE "the temporary text of section 348(e) ends inside this period, and the person began national-civic service on or after the day it ends"

-- One serving in national-civic service is within (e) for a period the temporary text reaches: a
-- period that ends by its expiry, or any period if the person "began service before that date"
-- ("before": a person who began on 31.8.2026 itself did not; fork F8). A month is wholly on one side
-- of 31 August; a quarter or a year can straddle it, and if it does for a person who began on or after
-- that day the temporary text reaches part of the period only, which (e) does not apportion: declined.
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), temporary text (source line 3769); s 1 "משרת בשירות לאומי–אזרחי" (source line 173)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(e) — the person serves in national-civic service in a period the temporary text reaches` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `the day the person began national-civic service, if serving in it`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST `the day service began` THEN
        BRANCH IF `the period ends by the expiry`                                                    THEN TRUE
               IF Day `the day service began` LESS THAN Day `the expiry`                             THEN TRUE
               IF `the period begins after the expiry`                                              THEN FALSE
               OTHERWISE `the temporary text of section 348(e) ends inside this period, and the person began national-civic service on or after the day it ends`
    WHERE
        `the expiry` MEANS `the expiry of the National-Civic Service Law, which ends the temporary text of section 348(e)`
        `the period ends by the expiry` MEANS
            `the month count of month` (`the last month of the period` (c's `period`)) `of` (c's `tax year`)
                AT MOST `the month count of month` (DATE_MONTH `the expiry`) `of` (DATE_YEAR `the expiry`)
        `the period begins after the expiry` MEANS
            `the month count of month` (`the first month of the period` (c's `period`)) `of` (c's `tax year`)
                GREATER THAN `the month count of month` (DATE_MONTH `the expiry`) `of` (DATE_YEAR `the expiry`)

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e), both texts (source lines 3768-3769)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(e) — the person is of a class (e) names, in the period` c MEANS
        `s 348(e) — the person is of a class both texts name` c
    OR  `s 348(e) — the person serves in national-civic service in a period the temporary text reaches` c

§§ `Which item of Schedule K is "for him"`

-- (b) applies "the minimum amount stated for him in Schedule K". The item follows from the column of
-- insured person, and for one who is neither, from (d) and (e): item 3 is "an insured person as stated
-- in s 348(d) and (e)", read as the classes those subsections name (fork F6). An employee or a
-- self-employed person keeps item 1 or 2 even if also within (e) (fork F7); where that makes a
-- difference, the rules below decline.
@ref National Insurance Law Schedule K column "בעד" (source lines 4757-4765); s 348(b), (d), (e) (source lines 3765-3769)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
GIVETH AN `An item of Schedule K`
`the item of Schedule K for` c MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `column`
    WHEN `an employee`            THEN `item 1, an employee`
    WHEN `a self-employed person` THEN `item 2, a self-employed person`
    OTHERWISE
        IF       c's `received unemployment benefit for a full month under Chapter G`
             OR  `s 348(e) — the person is of a class (e) names, in the period` c
        THEN `item 3, an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)`
        ELSE `item 4, another insured person`

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(a) (source line 3763); Schedule K
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule K maximum for` c `, under` f MEANS
    `the maximum income under Schedule K for` (`the item of Schedule K for` c) `, for` (c's `period`) `, under` f

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(b) (source line 3765); Schedule K
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule K minimum for` c `, under` f MEANS
    `the minimum income under Schedule K for` (`the item of Schedule K for` c) `, for` (c's `period`) `, under` f `and` (c's `the minimum wage applicable to the employee`)

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(d)-(e) and Schedule K item 3 (source lines 3767-3769, 4763-4764)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the Schedule K item 3 minimum for the period of` c `, under` f MEANS
    `the minimum income under Schedule K for` `item 3, an insured person as stated in section 348(d) and (e)` `, for` (c's `period`) `, under` f `and` NOTHING

§§ `348(a1) — income not from work, up to 25% of the average wage, is not taken into account`

-- src:3764 | (א1) לעניין דמי ביטוח המשתלמים לפי הוראות סעיף 335, לא תובא בחשבון ההכנסה של מבוטח מהמקורות המפורטים בסעיף 2 לפקודת מס הכנסה, שאינה הכנסה מעבודתו כעובד או כעובד עצמאי, אשר אינה פטורה מתשלום דמי ביטוח לפי סעיף 350 ואינה עולה על סכום השווה ל־25% מהשכר הממוצע.
-- "the income of an insured person from the sources in s 2 of the Income Tax Ordinance that is not
-- income from his work as an employee or self-employed, which is not exempt under s 350 and does not
-- exceed a sum equal to 25% of the average wage, shall not be taken into account."
-- READ AS a deduction: the part of that income up to the 25% sum is disregarded, as (a)'s "the amount
-- of the income exceeding the maximum" is the part above it (fork F3). The National Insurance
-- Institute's worked example does the same: rent of 12,000 in January 2026 is charged on 8,558
-- (12,000 less 3,442). The other reading, all or nothing, is below for comparison.
-- The 25% sum is stated with no period; it is a month's (25% of the average wage of the month), and
-- this row applies it to a month only (fork F4).
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(a1) (source line 3764)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 348(a1) states its sum without a period, and this row applies it to a month only` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 348(a1) states its sum without a period, and this row applies it to a month only"

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(a1) (source line 3764); s 1 "השכר הממוצע" (source lines 222-226)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348(a1) — the sum equal to 25% of the average wage, for the period of` c `, under` f MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `period`
    WHEN `a month of the tax year` m THEN 25% TIMES `the average wage of month` m `, under` f
    OTHERWISE `section 348(a1) states its sum without a period, and this row applies it to a month only`

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(a1) (source line 3764); NOTES.md fork F3
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348(a1) — the income not from work that is not taken into account, for` c `, under` f MEANS
    IF   `the income not from work` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE min `the income not from work` (`s 348(a1) — the sum equal to 25% of the average wage, for the period of` c `, under` f)
    WHERE
        `the income not from work` MEANS c's `income not from work in the period, not exempt under section 350`

-- The other reading of (a1), all or nothing: the income is disregarded only if it does not exceed the
-- sum, and then all of it. Not used by the rules below; the tests show where the two part.
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(a1) (source line 3764); NOTES.md fork F3, the reading not taken
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348(a1), read as all or nothing — the income not from work that is not taken into account, for` c `, under` f MEANS
    IF   `the income not from work` EQUALS 0
    THEN 0
    ELSE IF   `the income not from work` AT MOST (`s 348(a1) — the sum equal to 25% of the average wage, for the period of` c `, under` f)
         THEN `the income not from work`
         ELSE 0
    WHERE
        `the income not from work` MEANS c's `income not from work in the period, not exempt under section 350`

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(a1) (source line 3764)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348(a1) — the income taken into account, for` c `, under` f MEANS
        c's `income from work in the period`
    PLUS c's `income not from work in the period, not exempt under section 350`
    MINUS `s 348(a1) — the income not from work that is not taken into account, for` c `, under` f

§§ `348(a) — income above the maximum is not taken into account`

-- src:3763 | (א) לענין דמי ביטוח המשתלמים לפי הוראה מהוראות סעיף 335 לא יבוא בחשבון סכום ההכנסה של המבוטח העולה על הסכום המרבי המתקבל לפי האמור בלוח י״א.
-- "For contributions payable under any provision of s 335, the amount of the insured person's income
-- exceeding the maximum amount obtained under Schedule K shall not be taken into account."
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(a) (source line 3763)
GIVEN `the income`  IS A NUMBER
      `the maximum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348(a) — the income taken into account, of` `the income` `, with the maximum at` `the maximum` MEANS
    min `the income` `the maximum`

§§ `348(b) — no income, or less than the minimum: as if the minimum`

-- src:3765 | (ב) מבוטח שאין לו הכנסה או שהכנסתו אינה מגיעה לסכום המזערי האמור לגביו בלוח י״א, ישתלמו בעדו דמי הביטוח כאילו הכנסתו היתה הסכום המזערי האמור.
-- "An insured person who has no income, or whose income does not reach the minimum amount stated for
-- him in Schedule K: contributions are paid for him as if his income were that minimum amount."
-- "does not reach" is below it: at the minimum, the income is the income. s 350(c) (source line 3805,
-- not in this row) disapplies this subsection for some residents exempt under s 350(a); it does not
-- mention (d) or (e) (fork F18).
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(b) (source line 3765)
GIVEN `the income`  IS A NUMBER
      `the minimum` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(b) — no income, or an income that does not reach the minimum: of` `the income` `, with the minimum at` `the minimum` MEANS
    `the income` LESS THAN `the minimum`

@ref National Insurance Law ss 348(a) and (b) (source lines 3763, 3765); s 350(c) (source line 3805)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348(a) and (b) — the income on which contributions are computed, for` c `, under` f MEANS
    IF       NOT c's `section 350(c) disapplies section 348(b) to the person`
         AND `s 348(b) — no income, or an income that does not reach the minimum: of` `the income` `, with the minimum at` (`the Schedule K minimum for` c `, under` f)
    THEN `the Schedule K minimum for` c `, under` f
    ELSE `s 348(a) — the income taken into account, of` `the income` `, with the maximum at` (`the Schedule K maximum for` c `, under` f)
    WHERE
        `the income` MEANS `s 348(a1) — the income taken into account, for` c `, under` f

§§ `348(c) — the Minister may change the minimum amounts by order`

-- src:3766 | (ג) השר, באישור ועדת הכספים של הכנסת, רשאי לשנות בצו את הסכומים המזעריים האמורים בלוח י״א.
-- The power has a fallback: until an order is made, Schedule K's amounts stand. No order is in the
-- sources, so a period an order reaches is declined, and the power's own conditions are a test.
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(c) (source line 3766)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`an order under section 348(c) changed a minimum amount for this period, and no such order is encoded here` MEANS
    REFUSE "an order under section 348(c) changed a minimum amount for this period, and no such order is encoded here"

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(c) (source line 3766)
GIVEN o IS AN `An order changing the minimum amounts in Schedule K`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(c) — the order is within the Minister's power` o MEANS
        o's `made by the Minister`
    AND o's `approved by the Finance Committee of the Knesset`

§§ `348(d) — unemployment benefit for a full month`

-- src:3767 | (ד) מבוטח שקיבל דמי אבטלה לחודש מלא לפי פרק ז׳, ישלם דמי ביטוח כאילו היתה הכנסתו הסכום המזערי הקבוע בפרט 3 שבלוח י״א.
-- "An insured person who received unemployment benefit for a full month under Chapter G pays
-- contributions as if his income were the minimum amount fixed in item 3 of Schedule K."
-- Unlike (b) and (e), (d) has no condition "who has no income or whose income does not reach". Read as
-- a deeming, the month's income is the item 3 minimum whatever it was; read as a floor, like (e), it is
-- the item 3 minimum only if the income is below it. The two readings give the same answer when the
-- income does not exceed the item 3 minimum, and that is the only case answered (fork F5). (d) speaks
-- of a full month, so a quarter or a year is not answered either; and an employee or a self-employed
-- person in receipt is not, because (d) does not say how its deeming meets income from that work
-- (fork F7).
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(d) (source line 3767)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 348(d) is stated for a full month` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 348(d) is stated for a full month"

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(d) (source line 3767); NOTES.md fork F5
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 348(d) as a deeming and as a floor give different answers when the income exceeds the item 3 minimum` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 348(d) as a deeming and as a floor give different answers when the income exceeds the item 3 minimum"

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(d) (source line 3767); NOTES.md fork F7
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 348(d) does not say how its deeming meets income as an employee or as a self-employed person` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 348(d) does not say how its deeming meets income as an employee or as a self-employed person"

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(d) (source line 3767)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348(d) — the income on which contributions are computed, for` c `, under` f MEANS
    CONSIDER c's `period`
    WHEN `a month of the tax year` m THEN
        BRANCH IF NOT (c's `column` EQUALS `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed`)
                  THEN `section 348(d) does not say how its deeming meets income as an employee or as a self-employed person`
               IF `s 348(a1) — the income taken into account, for` c `, under` f AT MOST `the item 3 minimum`
                  THEN `the item 3 minimum`
               OTHERWISE `section 348(d) as a deeming and as a floor give different answers when the income exceeds the item 3 minimum`
    OTHERWISE `section 348(d) is stated for a full month`
    WHERE
        `the item 3 minimum` MEANS `the Schedule K item 3 minimum for the period of` c `, under` f

§§ `348(e) — volunteers, yeshiva students, civil and national-civic service: as if the item 3 minimum`

-- "... who has no income or whose income does not reach the minimum amount stated in item 3 of
-- Schedule K: their income is regarded as that minimum amount." For one who is neither employee nor
-- self-employed this is (b) with item 3, and gives the same answer; it is written separately because
-- it is a separate subsection, s 350(c) does not reach it, and it names an employee or a self-employed
-- person too, for whom item 1 or 2 is "the minimum stated for him" under (b). Where (e) and (b) then
-- disagree, it is declined (fork F7).
@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e) (source lines 3768-3769); NOTES.md fork F7
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`section 348(e) and section 348(b) give different minimums for an employee or a self-employed person in a class (e) names` MEANS
    REFUSE "section 348(e) and section 348(b) give different minimums for an employee or a self-employed person in a class (e) names"

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e) (source lines 3768-3769)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 348(e) — a person of a class (e) names, with no income or an income that does not reach the item 3 minimum:` c `, under` f MEANS
        `s 348(e) — the person is of a class (e) names, in the period` c
    AND `s 348(a1) — the income taken into account, for` c `, under` f LESS THAN `the Schedule K item 3 minimum for the period of` c `, under` f

@ref National Insurance Law s 348(e) (source lines 3768-3769)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348(e) — the income regarded as the item 3 minimum, for` c `, under` f MEANS
    IF   c's `column` EQUALS `an insured person who is neither an employee nor self-employed`
    THEN `the Schedule K item 3 minimum for the period of` c `, under` f
    ELSE `section 348(e) and section 348(b) give different minimums for an employee or a self-employed person in a class (e) names`

§§ `Section 348 — the income on which contributions are computed`

-- The section as a whole, for a period from January 2026 (assumption A1), in the order (c), (d), (e),
-- then (a1), (a) and (b).
@ref National Insurance Law s 348 (source lines 3762-3769); Schedule K (source lines 4751-4773)
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
      f IS A `The figures Schedule K reads for a tax year`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348 — the income on which contributions are computed, for` c `, under` f MEANS
    BRANCH IF c's `tax year` LESS THAN 2026
              THEN `this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only`
           IF NOT (f's `tax year` EQUALS c's `tax year`)
              THEN `the figures given are for another tax year than the case`
           IF c's `an order under section 348(c) has changed a minimum amount for the period`
              THEN `an order under section 348(c) changed a minimum amount for this period, and no such order is encoded here`
           IF c's `received unemployment benefit for a full month under Chapter G`
              THEN `s 348(d) — the income on which contributions are computed, for` c `, under` f
           IF `s 348(e) — a person of a class (e) names, with no income or an income that does not reach the item 3 minimum:` c `, under` f
              THEN `s 348(e) — the income regarded as the item 3 minimum, for` c `, under` f
           OTHERWISE `s 348(a) and (b) — the income on which contributions are computed, for` c `, under` f

-- The same, with the figures for the case's tax year as published (2026 only).
@ref National Insurance Law s 348 (source lines 3762-3769); Schedule K; National Insurance Institute figures for 2026
GIVEN c IS AN `An insured person's period under section 348`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 348 — the income on which contributions are computed, for` c MEANS
    IF   c's `tax year` LESS THAN 2026
    THEN `this row answers contribution periods from January 2026 only`
    ELSE `s 348 — the income on which contributions are computed, for` c `, under` (`the figures Schedule K reads for the tax year` (c's `tax year`))
